IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-persons`
IMPORT `uc1-common`
IMPORT `uc1-part2-age-and-place`

-- Tests of uc1-part2-age-and-place.l4 (regulations 8 to 11). Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the
-- regulation named in the comment beside it, and none was copied from the output of the rule. The builders below take one
-- BOOLEAN per field, in the order the comment above each lists; a fixture names the case it stands for.

-- Arguments of `test — young person who may be a care leaver`, in order:
--   1. nation in which the care is provided
--   2. the person is an eligible child for the purposes of paragraph 19B of Schedule 2 to the Children ...
--   3. the person is under the age of 18
--   4. the person is looked after by a local authority
--   5. the person has ceased to be looked after by a local authority but is a person to whom a local au...
--   6. since reaching the age of 14 the person has been looked after by a local authority for a period ...
--   7. the person is a category 1 young person or category 2 young person within the meaning of section...
GIVEN a1 IS A `Nation of Great Britain`
      a2 IS A BOOLEAN
      a3 IS A BOOLEAN
      a4 IS A BOOLEAN
      a5 IS A BOOLEAN
      a6 IS A BOOLEAN
      a7 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Young person who may be a care leaver`
`test — young person who may be a care leaver` a1 a2 a3 a4 a5 a6 a7 MEANS
    `Young person who may be a care leaver` WITH
        `nation in which the care is provided` IS a1
        `the person is an eligible child for the purposes of paragraph 19B of Schedule 2 to the Children Act 1989, or a relevant child for the purposes of section 23A of that Act` IS a2
        `the person is under the age of 18` IS a3
        `the person is looked after by a local authority` IS a4
        `the person has ceased to be looked after by a local authority but is a person to whom a local authority in Scotland is obliged to provide advice and assistance in terms of section 29(1) of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995, or is being provided with continuing care under section 26A of that Act` IS a5
        `since reaching the age of 14 the person has been looked after by a local authority for a period of, or periods totalling, 3 months or more, excluding any period where the person has been placed with a member of their family` IS a6
        `the person is a category 1 young person or category 2 young person within the meaning of section 104(2) of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014` IS a7

`an English eligible child` MEANS `test — young person who may be a care leaver` England TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`an English young person with no care leaver status` MEANS `test — young person who may be a care leaver` England FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`an English young person with only a Welsh category` MEANS `test — young person who may be a care leaver` England FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
`a Welsh category young person` MEANS `test — young person who may be a care leaver` Wales FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
`a Welsh young person with only the English status` MEANS `test — young person who may be a care leaver` Wales TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a Scottish young person under 18 who is looked after and was looked after for 3 months` MEANS `test — young person who may be a care leaver` Scotland FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`a Scottish young person under 18 owed advice and assistance who was looked after for 3 months` MEANS `test — young person who may be a care leaver` Scotland FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
`a Scottish young person under 18 who is looked after but not for 3 months` MEANS `test — young person who may be a care leaver` Scotland FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a Scottish young person aged 18 who is looked after for 3 months` MEANS `test — young person who may be a care leaver` Scotland FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`a Scottish young person under 18 neither looked after nor owed advice` MEANS `test — young person who may be a care leaver` Scotland FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE

-- Arguments of `test — right to reside`, in order:
--   1. the right exists by virtue of, or in accordance with, regulation 13 of the EEA Regulations
--   2. the right exists under regulation 14 of the EEA Regulations only because the person is a qualifi...
--   3. the right exists under regulation 14 of the EEA Regulations only because the person is a family ...
--   4. the right exists under regulation 16 of the EEA Regulations only because the person satisfies th...
--   5. the person has been granted limited leave under the Immigration Act 1971 by virtue of Appendix E...
--   6. the person has been granted limited leave under the Immigration Act 1971 by virtue of being a pe...
--   7. the person has been granted limited leave under the Immigration Act 1971 by virtue of having arr...
--   8. the right was granted by virtue of being a family member of a relevant person of Northern Irelan...
--   9. the person would have a right to reside under the EEA Regulations if the relevant person of Nort...
--   10. that right to reside would fall within paragraph (3)(a) or (b)
GIVEN a1 IS A BOOLEAN
      a2 IS A BOOLEAN
      a3 IS A BOOLEAN
      a4 IS A BOOLEAN
      a5 IS A BOOLEAN
      a6 IS A BOOLEAN
      a7 IS A BOOLEAN
      a8 IS A BOOLEAN
      a9 IS A BOOLEAN
      a10 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Right to reside`
`test — right to reside` a1 a2 a3 a4 a5 a6 a7 a8 a9 a10 MEANS
    `Right to reside` WITH
        `the right exists by virtue of, or in accordance with, regulation 13 of the EEA Regulations` IS a1
        `the right exists under regulation 14 of the EEA Regulations only because the person is a qualified person for the purposes of regulation 6(1) of those Regulations as a jobseeker` IS a2
        `the right exists under regulation 14 of the EEA Regulations only because the person is a family member of such a jobseeker` IS a3
        `the right exists under regulation 16 of the EEA Regulations only because the person satisfies the criteria in regulation 16(5) of those Regulations` IS a4
        `the person has been granted limited leave under the Immigration Act 1971 by virtue of Appendix EU to the immigration rules` IS a5
        `the person has been granted limited leave under the Immigration Act 1971 by virtue of being a person with a Zambrano right to reside as defined in Annex 1 of Appendix EU` IS a6
        `the person has been granted limited leave under the Immigration Act 1971 by virtue of having arrived in the United Kingdom with an entry clearance that was granted under Appendix EU (Family Permit)` IS a7
        `the right was granted by virtue of being a family member of a relevant person of Northern Ireland` IS a8
        `the person would have a right to reside under the EEA Regulations if the relevant person of Northern Ireland were an EEA national` IS a9
        `that right to reside would fall within paragraph (3)(a) or (b)` IS a10

`a right to reside of no excluded kind` MEANS `test — right to reside` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a right under regulation 13 of the EEA Regulations` MEANS `test — right to reside` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a right under regulation 14 only as a jobseeker` MEANS `test — right to reside` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a right under regulation 14 only as a family member of a jobseeker` MEANS `test — right to reside` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a right under regulation 16 only by the criteria in regulation 16(5)` MEANS `test — right to reside` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`limited leave by virtue of Appendix EU` MEANS `test — right to reside` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`limited leave as a person with a Zambrano right` MEANS `test — right to reside` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`limited leave with an Appendix EU (Family Permit) entry clearance` MEANS `test — right to reside` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`limited leave by Appendix EU as a family member of a relevant person of Northern Ireland` MEANS `test — right to reside` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
`limited leave by Appendix EU as a family member of a relevant person of Northern Ireland whose right falls within paragraph (3)(a) or (b)` MEANS `test — right to reside` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
`limited leave by Appendix EU as a family member of a relevant person of Northern Ireland who would have no right under the EEA Regulations` MEANS `test — right to reside` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`limited leave as a Zambrano right holder who is a family member of a relevant person of Northern Ireland` MEANS `test — right to reside` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE

-- Arguments of `test — person who may be within regulation 9(4)(za) to (zg)`, in order:
--   1. the person has been granted leave in accordance with the immigration rules made under section 3(...
--   2. the person has been granted leave in accordance with the immigration rules made under section 3(...
--   3. the person is in Great Britain and left Afghanistan in connection with the collapse of the Afgha...
--   4. the person was residing in Ukraine immediately before 1st January 2022 and left Ukraine in conne...
--   5. the person was residing in Sudan before 15th April 2023 and left Sudan in connection with the vi...
--   6. the person was residing in Israel, the West Bank, the Gaza Strip, East Jerusalem, the Golan Heig...
--   7. the person has been granted leave in accordance with immigration rules made under section 3(2) o...
--   8. the person has a right of abode in the United Kingdom within the meaning given in section 2 of t...
--   9. the person does not require leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom in accordance with se...
--   10. the person was residing in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His M...
--   11. the person has left that country or territory and is present in Great Britain
--   12. the person has leave on a discretionary basis outside of rules made under section 3(2) of the Im...
--   13. the person, as part of a safe and legal humanitarian immigration route, has leave to enter or re...
--   14. the person has been granted, or is deemed to have been granted, leave outside the rules made und...
GIVEN a1 IS A BOOLEAN
      a2 IS A BOOLEAN
      a3 IS A BOOLEAN
      a4 IS A BOOLEAN
      a5 IS A BOOLEAN
      a6 IS A BOOLEAN
      a7 IS A BOOLEAN
      a8 IS A BOOLEAN
      a9 IS A BOOLEAN
      a10 IS A BOOLEAN
      a11 IS A BOOLEAN
      a12 IS A BOOLEAN
      a13 IS A BOOLEAN
      a14 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Person who may be within regulation 9(4)(za) to (zg)`
`test — person who may be within regulation 9(4)(za) to (zg)` a1 a2 a3 a4 a5 a6 a7 a8 a9 a10 a11 a12 a13 a14 MEANS
    `Person who may be within regulation 9(4)(za) to (zg)` WITH
        `the person has been granted leave in accordance with the immigration rules made under section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971 by virtue of the Afghan Relocations and Assistance Policy` IS a1
        `the person has been granted leave in accordance with the immigration rules made under section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971 by virtue of the previous scheme for locally-employed staff in Afghanistan (the ex-gratia scheme)` IS a2
        `the person is in Great Britain and left Afghanistan in connection with the collapse of the Afghan government that took place on 15th August 2021` IS a3
        `the person was residing in Ukraine immediately before 1st January 2022 and left Ukraine in connection with the Russian invasion which took place on 24th February 2022` IS a4
        `the person was residing in Sudan before 15th April 2023 and left Sudan in connection with the violence which rapidly escalated on 15th April 2023 in Khartoum and across Sudan` IS a5
        `the person was residing in Israel, the West Bank, the Gaza Strip, East Jerusalem, the Golan Heights or Lebanon immediately before 7th October 2023 and left in connection with the Hamas terrorist attack in Israel on 7th October 2023 or the violence which rapidly escalated in the region following the attack` IS a6
        `the person has been granted leave in accordance with immigration rules made under section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971` IS a7
        `the person has a right of abode in the United Kingdom within the meaning given in section 2 of the Immigration Act 1971` IS a8
        `the person does not require leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom in accordance with section 3ZA of the Immigration Act 1971` IS a9
        `the person was residing in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty's Government provided public information to advise British nationals to leave it, or arranged the evacuation of British nationals from it` IS a10
        `the person has left that country or territory and is present in Great Britain` IS a11
        `the person has leave on a discretionary basis outside of rules made under section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971` IS a12
        `the person, as part of a safe and legal humanitarian immigration route, has leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom in accordance with immigration rules made under section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971 or leave on a discretionary basis outside of rules` IS a13
        `the person has been granted, or is deemed to have been granted, leave outside the rules made under section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971` IS a14

`leave under the Afghan Relocations and Assistance Policy` MEANS `test — person who may be within regulation 9(4)(za) to (zg)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`leave under the ex-gratia scheme` MEANS `test — person who may be within regulation 9(4)(za) to (zg)` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`no Afghan leave` MEANS `test — person who may be within regulation 9(4)(za) to (zg)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a person who left Afghanistan on the collapse of its government` MEANS `test — person who may be within regulation 9(4)(za) to (zg)` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a person who left Afghanistan and has Afghan Relocations leave` MEANS `test — person who may be within regulation 9(4)(za) to (zg)` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a person who left Ukraine with leave` MEANS `test — person who may be within regulation 9(4)(za) to (zg)` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a person who left Ukraine with a right of abode` MEANS `test — person who may be within regulation 9(4)(za) to (zg)` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a person who left Ukraine and needs no leave` MEANS `test — person who may be within regulation 9(4)(za) to (zg)` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a person who left Ukraine with no leave, abode or exemption` MEANS `test — person who may be within regulation 9(4)(za) to (zg)` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a person with leave who did not leave Ukraine` MEANS `test — person who may be within regulation 9(4)(za) to (zg)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a person who left Sudan with leave` MEANS `test — person who may be within regulation 9(4)(za) to (zg)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a person who left Sudan with no leave, abode or exemption` MEANS `test — person who may be within regulation 9(4)(za) to (zg)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a person who left Israel or the region and needs no leave` MEANS `test — person who may be within regulation 9(4)(za) to (zg)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a person who left Israel or the region with no leave, abode or exemption` MEANS `test — person who may be within regulation 9(4)(za) to (zg)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a person evacuated who has a right of abode` MEANS `test — person who may be within regulation 9(4)(za) to (zg)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a person evacuated who needs no leave` MEANS `test — person who may be within regulation 9(4)(za) to (zg)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a person evacuated who has leave under the rules` MEANS `test — person who may be within regulation 9(4)(za) to (zg)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a person evacuated who has discretionary leave` MEANS `test — person who may be within regulation 9(4)(za) to (zg)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`a person evacuated with no leave of any kind` MEANS `test — person who may be within regulation 9(4)(za) to (zg)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a person evacuated who has not left the country` MEANS `test — person who may be within regulation 9(4)(za) to (zg)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a person with leave on a safe and legal humanitarian route` MEANS `test — person who may be within regulation 9(4)(za) to (zg)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`a person granted leave outside the rules` MEANS `test — person who may be within regulation 9(4)(za) to (zg)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE

-- Arguments of `test — person who may be within the remaining limbs of regulation 9(4)`, in order:
--   1. the person is a qualified person for the purposes of regulation 6 of the EEA Regulations as a wo...
--   2. the person is a family member of a person referred to in sub-paragraph (a)
--   3. the person has a right to reside permanently in the United Kingdom by virtue of regulation 15(1)...
--   4. the person is a family member of a relevant person of Northern Ireland, with a right to reside w...
--   5. the relevant person of Northern Ireland falls within paragraph (4)(a), or would do so but for th...
--   6. the person is a frontier worker within the meaning of regulation 3 of the Citizens' Rights (Fron...
--   7. the person is a family member of a person referred to in sub-paragraph (cb)
--   8. the person has been granted limited leave to enter, or remain in, the United Kingdom by virtue o...
--   9. the person is a refugee within the definition in Article 1 of the Convention relating to the Sta...
--   10. the person has humanitarian protection granted under the immigration rules
--   11. the person is not a person subject to immigration control within the meaning of section 115(9) o...
GIVEN a1 IS A BOOLEAN
      a2 IS A BOOLEAN
      a3 IS A BOOLEAN
      a4 IS A BOOLEAN
      a5 IS A BOOLEAN
      a6 IS A BOOLEAN
      a7 IS A BOOLEAN
      a8 IS A BOOLEAN
      a9 IS A BOOLEAN
      a10 IS A BOOLEAN
      a11 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Person who may be within the remaining limbs of regulation 9(4)`
`test — person who may be within the remaining limbs of regulation 9(4)` a1 a2 a3 a4 a5 a6 a7 a8 a9 a10 a11 MEANS
    `Person who may be within the remaining limbs of regulation 9(4)` WITH
        `the person is a qualified person for the purposes of regulation 6 of the EEA Regulations as a worker or a self-employed person` IS a1
        `the person is a family member of a person referred to in sub-paragraph (a)` IS a2
        `the person has a right to reside permanently in the United Kingdom by virtue of regulation 15(1)(c), (d) or (e) of the EEA Regulations` IS a3
        `the person is a family member of a relevant person of Northern Ireland, with a right to reside which falls within paragraph (3)(c)(i)` IS a4
        `the relevant person of Northern Ireland falls within paragraph (4)(a), or would do so but for the fact that they are not an EEA national` IS a5
        `the person is a frontier worker within the meaning of regulation 3 of the Citizens' Rights (Frontier Workers) (EU Exit) Regulations 2020` IS a6
        `the person is a family member of a person referred to in sub-paragraph (cb)` IS a7
        `the person has been granted limited leave to enter, or remain in, the United Kingdom by virtue of Appendix EU to the immigration rules made under section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971` IS a8
        `the person is a refugee within the definition in Article 1 of the Convention relating to the Status of Refugees done at Geneva on 28th July 1951, as extended by Article 1(2) of the Protocol relating to the Status of Refugees done at New York on 31st January 1967` IS a9
        `the person has humanitarian protection granted under the immigration rules` IS a10
        `the person is not a person subject to immigration control within the meaning of section 115(9) of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 and is in the United Kingdom as a result of their deportation, expulsion or other removal by compulsion of law from another country to the United Kingdom` IS a11

`a qualified person as a worker or self-employed person` MEANS `test — person who may be within the remaining limbs of regulation 9(4)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a family member of a qualified person` MEANS `test — person who may be within the remaining limbs of regulation 9(4)` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a person with a right to reside permanently` MEANS `test — person who may be within the remaining limbs of regulation 9(4)` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a family member of a relevant person of Northern Ireland alone` MEANS `test — person who may be within the remaining limbs of regulation 9(4)` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a family member of a relevant person of Northern Ireland who falls within paragraph (4)(a)` MEANS `test — person who may be within the remaining limbs of regulation 9(4)` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`only the status of the relevant person of Northern Ireland` MEANS `test — person who may be within the remaining limbs of regulation 9(4)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a frontier worker` MEANS `test — person who may be within the remaining limbs of regulation 9(4)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a family member of a frontier worker alone` MEANS `test — person who may be within the remaining limbs of regulation 9(4)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a family member of a frontier worker with Appendix EU limited leave` MEANS `test — person who may be within the remaining limbs of regulation 9(4)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`limited leave under Appendix EU alone` MEANS `test — person who may be within the remaining limbs of regulation 9(4)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a refugee` MEANS `test — person who may be within the remaining limbs of regulation 9(4)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`a person with humanitarian protection` MEANS `test — person who may be within the remaining limbs of regulation 9(4)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`a person removed to the United Kingdom by compulsion of law` MEANS `test — person who may be within the remaining limbs of regulation 9(4)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
`a person within none of the remaining limbs` MEANS `test — person who may be within the remaining limbs of regulation 9(4)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- Arguments of `test — person who may be posted overseas`, in order:
--   1. the person holds an office or employment under the Crown
--   2. the person is a member of Her Majesty's forces within the meaning of the Armed Forces Act 2006
--   3. the person is performing overseas the duties of a Crown servant or member of Her Majesty's force...
--   4. the person was, immediately before their posting or the first of consecutive postings, habituall...
GIVEN a1 IS A BOOLEAN
      a2 IS A BOOLEAN
      a3 IS A BOOLEAN
      a4 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Person who may be posted overseas`
`test — person who may be posted overseas` a1 a2 a3 a4 MEANS
    `Person who may be posted overseas` WITH
        `the person holds an office or employment under the Crown` IS a1
        `the person is a member of Her Majesty's forces within the meaning of the Armed Forces Act 2006` IS a2
        `the person is performing overseas the duties of a Crown servant or member of Her Majesty's forces` IS a3
        `the person was, immediately before their posting or the first of consecutive postings, habitually resident in the United Kingdom` IS a4

`a Crown servant performing duties overseas who was habitually resident in the United Kingdom` MEANS `test — person who may be posted overseas` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
`a member of the forces performing duties overseas who was habitually resident in the United Kingdom` MEANS `test — person who may be posted overseas` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
`a person who is neither a Crown servant nor a member of the forces` MEANS `test — person who may be posted overseas` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
`a Crown servant not performing duties overseas` MEANS `test — person who may be posted overseas` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
`a Crown servant who was not habitually resident in the United Kingdom` MEANS `test — person who may be posted overseas` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE

-- Arguments of `test — person who may have the minimum age of 16`, in order:
--   1. the person has limited capability for work
--   2. the person is awaiting an assessment under Part 5 to determine whether the person has limited ca...
--   3. the person has a statement given in accordance with the Medical Evidence Regulations which provi...
--   4. the person has regular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person
--   5. the person is responsible for a child
--   6. the person is a member of a couple the other member of which is responsible for a child or a qua...
--   7. the other member meets the basic conditions in section 4 of the Act
--   8. the person is pregnant, and it is 11 weeks or less before her expected week of confinement, or w...
--   9. the person is without parental support
--   10. the person is a care leaver
GIVEN a1 IS A BOOLEAN
      a2 IS A BOOLEAN
      a3 IS A BOOLEAN
      a4 IS A BOOLEAN
      a5 IS A BOOLEAN
      a6 IS A BOOLEAN
      a7 IS A BOOLEAN
      a8 IS A BOOLEAN
      a9 IS A BOOLEAN
      a10 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Person who may have the minimum age of 16`
`test — person who may have the minimum age of 16` a1 a2 a3 a4 a5 a6 a7 a8 a9 a10 MEANS
    `Person who may have the minimum age of 16` WITH
        `the person has limited capability for work` IS a1
        `the person is awaiting an assessment under Part 5 to determine whether the person has limited capability for work` IS a2
        `the person has a statement given in accordance with the Medical Evidence Regulations which provides that the person is not fit for work` IS a3
        `the person has regular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person` IS a4
        `the person is responsible for a child` IS a5
        `the person is a member of a couple the other member of which is responsible for a child or a qualifying young person` IS a6
        `the other member meets the basic conditions in section 4 of the Act` IS a7
        `the person is pregnant, and it is 11 weeks or less before her expected week of confinement, or was pregnant and it is 15 weeks or less since the date of her confinement` IS a8
        `the person is without parental support` IS a9
        `the person is a care leaver` IS a10

`a person with limited capability for work` MEANS `test — person who may have the minimum age of 16` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a person with limited capability for work who is a care leaver` MEANS `test — person who may have the minimum age of 16` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
`a person awaiting an assessment with a statement of unfitness` MEANS `test — person who may have the minimum age of 16` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a person awaiting an assessment without a statement` MEANS `test — person who may have the minimum age of 16` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a person with a statement but not awaiting an assessment` MEANS `test — person who may have the minimum age of 16` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a carer of a severely disabled person` MEANS `test — person who may have the minimum age of 16` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a carer of a severely disabled person who is a care leaver` MEANS `test — person who may have the minimum age of 16` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
`a person responsible for a child` MEANS `test — person who may have the minimum age of 16` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a care leaver responsible for a child` MEANS `test — person who may have the minimum age of 16` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
`a member of a couple whose partner is responsible for a child and meets the basic conditions` MEANS `test — person who may have the minimum age of 16` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a member of a couple whose partner is responsible for a child but does not meet the basic conditions` MEANS `test — person who may have the minimum age of 16` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a person whose partner meets the basic conditions but is responsible for no child` MEANS `test — person who may have the minimum age of 16` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a pregnant person` MEANS `test — person who may have the minimum age of 16` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`a pregnant care leaver` MEANS `test — person who may have the minimum age of 16` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE
`a person without parental support` MEANS `test — person who may have the minimum age of 16` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`a care leaver without parental support` MEANS `test — person who may have the minimum age of 16` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
`a person with no ground for the minimum age of 16` MEANS `test — person who may have the minimum age of 16` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- Arguments of `test — person who may be within regulation 11(4A)`, in order:
--   1. the person was present in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Ma...
--   2. paragraphs (1)(a), (b)(i), (b)(ii) or (2) applied to the person when the public information was ...
--   3. the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to expect the person to return...
--   4. the person did not enter that country or territory when His Majesty's Government's public inform...
GIVEN a1 IS A BOOLEAN
      a2 IS A BOOLEAN
      a3 IS A BOOLEAN
      a4 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Person who may be within regulation 11(4A)`
`test — person who may be within regulation 11(4A)` a1 a2 a3 a4 MEANS
    `Person who may be within regulation 11(4A)` WITH
        `the person was present in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty's Government provided public information to advise British nationals to leave it, or arranged the evacuation of British nationals from it` IS a1
        `paragraphs (1)(a), (b)(i), (b)(ii) or (2) applied to the person when the public information was issued or the evacuation began` IS a2
        `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to expect the person to return, or to have returned, to Great Britain` IS a3
        `the person did not enter that country or territory when His Majesty's Government's public information was to advise British nationals to leave it` IS a4

`a person within every limb of paragraph (4A)` MEANS `test — person who may be within regulation 11(4A)` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
`a person not present abroad before the advice` MEANS `test — person who may be within regulation 11(4A)` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
`a person to whom no earlier paragraph applied` MEANS `test — person who may be within regulation 11(4A)` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
`a person the Secretary of State is not satisfied about` MEANS `test — person who may be within regulation 11(4A)` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
`a person who entered the country after the advice to leave` MEANS `test — person who may be within regulation 11(4A)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE

-- Arguments of `test — reason for a temporary absence from Great Britain`, in order:
--   1. the absence is solely in connection with the person undergoing treatment for an illness or physi...
--   2. the absence is solely in connection with the person undergoing medically approved convalescence ...
--   3. the absence is solely in connection with the person accompanying their partner or a child or qua...
--   4. the person is a mariner
--   5. the person is a continental shelf worker who is in a designated area or a prescribed area
GIVEN a1 IS A BOOLEAN
      a2 IS A BOOLEAN
      a3 IS A BOOLEAN
      a4 IS A BOOLEAN
      a5 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Reason for a temporary absence from Great Britain`
`test — reason for a temporary absence from Great Britain` a1 a2 a3 a4 a5 MEANS
    `Reason for a temporary absence from Great Britain` WITH
        `the absence is solely in connection with the person undergoing treatment for an illness or physical or mental impairment by, or under the supervision of, a qualified practitioner` IS a1
        `the absence is solely in connection with the person undergoing medically approved convalescence or care as a result of treatment for an illness or physical or mental impairment, where the person had that illness or impairment before leaving Great Britain` IS a2
        `the absence is solely in connection with the person accompanying their partner or a child or qualifying young person for whom they are responsible for treatment or convalescence or care as mentioned in sub-paragraph (a)` IS a3
        `the person is a mariner` IS a4
        `the person is a continental shelf worker who is in a designated area or a prescribed area` IS a5

`an absence for treatment` MEANS `test — reason for a temporary absence from Great Britain` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`an absence for convalescence` MEANS `test — reason for a temporary absence from Great Britain` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`an absence accompanying a family member for treatment` MEANS `test — reason for a temporary absence from Great Britain` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`an absence of a mariner` MEANS `test — reason for a temporary absence from Great Britain` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`an absence of a continental shelf worker` MEANS `test — reason for a temporary absence from Great Britain` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
`an absence for no listed reason` MEANS `test — reason for a temporary absence from Great Britain` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE


