-- Regulation 11: absences from Great Britain, from 1 January 2025.
GIVEN lasted IS A DATE
      expected IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Absence that is measured against a limit`
`test — absence from 1 January 2025` lasted expected MEANS
    `Absence that is measured against a limit` WITH
        `first day of the absence` IS YearMonthDay 2025 1 1
        `day to which the absence has lasted` IS lasted
        `expected last day of the absence` IS expected
`an absence expected to end on 1 February 2025` MEANS `test — absence from 1 January 2025` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 2 1)
`an absence expected to end on 2 February 2025` MEANS `test — absence from 1 January 2025` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 2 2)
`an absence expected to end on 1 March 2025` MEANS `test — absence from 1 January 2025` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1)
`an absence expected to end on 2 March 2025` MEANS `test — absence from 1 January 2025` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 2)
`an absence expected to end on 1 July 2025` MEANS `test — absence from 1 January 2025` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1)
`an absence expected to end on 2 July 2025` MEANS `test — absence from 1 January 2025` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 7 2)
`an absence that has lasted to 1 July 2025` MEANS `test — absence from 1 January 2025` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1)
`an absence that has lasted to 2 July 2025` MEANS `test — absence from 1 January 2025` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 2) (YearMonthDay 2025 7 2)

